---
# kernscope clang-tidy configuration (committed, F2 prerequisite).
#
# Philosophy: bug-focused, CI-enforceable. WarningsAsErrors: '*' means a
# clang-tidy finding is a build failure, so every ENABLED check must pull its
# weight on kernel-style numeric code. Checks that mostly report style
# preference, or produce too many false positives on this codebase, are
# DISABLED — with the rationale documented next to each. This is a principled
# calibration (validated against a full libs/ + tools/ run), not a blanket
# disable.
#
# Enabled families (bug signal):
#   bugprone-*        real correctness traps
#   performance-*     real performance issues (incl. enum size)
#   clang-analyzer-*  static-analyzer interprocedural bugs
#   portability-*     real portability issues
#   misc-*            minus const-correctness (style) and the noisy items
#   readability-*     minus the mega-noise items (pure style / kernel idiom)
#
# Disabled checks + rationale:
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: same-type adjacent parameters are
#     pervasive in numeric kernels (int row, int col); renaming would not
#     improve bug detection here.
#   bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result: int * int -> size_t
#     widening is deliberate in kernel sizing math; forcing casts everywhere
#     obscures the numeric code this suite exists to analyze.
#   misc-const-correctness: style preference; ~354 findings of const-churn
#     with no bug signal (kernel code mutates locals freely by design).
#   misc-include-cleaner: include-what-you-use churn over generated and
#     vendor-adjacent TUs; include discipline is already enforced by
#     -Wall -Wextra -Werror at build time.
#   misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes: plain-data structs (metric
#     records, config bundles) are public-by-design in this codebase.
#   portability-avoid-pragma-once: tools/verify + tools/pass plugin headers
#     deliberately use #pragma once — they are consumed by LLVM's plugin
#     tooling and compiled by several compilers (gcc/clang/hipcc/nvcc), where
#     #pragma once is universally supported and guard-symbol collisions are a
#     real hazard; converting them is style churn with no bug value.
#   readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator: nested ternaries in
#     numeric kernels are idiomatic and readable here; style preference only.
#   readability-braces-around-statements: pure style; guard-clause style is
#     the codebase convention (~1,743 findings would bury every real bug).
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity: kernel bodies with many
#     branches are the substance of the code, not a smell.
#   readability-identifier-length: 1-char loop/index variables (i, j, k, n)
#     are the GPU-kernel idiom this project analyzes.
#   readability-implicit-bool-conversion: `if (ptr)` / `if (count)` kernel
#     idiom; forcing explicit comparisons is churn, not safety (~343 findings).
#   readability-magic-numbers: kernel numeric constants are the workload, not
#     magic; literals like 32 (warp size) are meaningful by domain convention.
#   readability-suspicious-call-argument: argument-order false positives on
#     numeric kernels drown the real findings.
#   readability-uppercase-literal-suffix: pure style (1.0f vs 1.0F); no bug
#     signal in either direction (~265 findings).
#
# WarningsAsErrors: '*' matches the build's -Wall -Wextra -Werror guarantee:
# a clang-tidy finding is a build failure, not a suggestion.
Checks: >-
  -*,bugprone-*,performance-*,clang-analyzer-*,portability-*,misc-*,readability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -misc-const-correctness,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -readability-avoid-nested-conditional-operator,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-suspicious-call-argument,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(libs|tools|tests)/.*'
FormatStyle: none
...
